.Dd October 3, 2026
.Dt MOUNT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount ,
.Nm umount
.Nd attach and detach a file system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm mount
.Nm mount
.Op Ar options
.Op Fl o Ar option
.Ar device directory
.Nm umount
.Op Ar options
.Ar filesystem Ns | Ns Ar directory
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm mount
and
.Nm umount
commands are BusyBox applets using this kernel's mount interfaces.
With no arguments,
.Nm mount
lists mounts from
.Pa /proc/mounts .
Mounting requires effective user ID 0.
.Pp
The kernel accepts the types
.Ql vfat ,
.Ql exfat ,
.Ql ext2 ,
and
.Ql krffs .
The kernel places the synthetic
.Ql devfs
and
.Ql proc
mounts itself.
The target must be a directory other than the root directory or an
existing mount point.
.Pp
The source can be a partition node
.Pa /dev/diskNpM ,
a whole disk
.Pa /dev/diskN
containing a volume without a partition table,
a loop device
.Pa /dev/loopN ,
or
.Pa /dev/bootpart .
The source's sector range is reserved for the life of the mount.
Another mount on that range, or an open descriptor that permits writes
to a disk or partition device whose sector range overlaps it, prevents the
mount.
.Pp
BusyBox can resolve
.Ql LABEL=
and
.Ql UUID=
sources through blkid.
This build has no mount helpers, mtab support, or
.Fl o Cm loop
support.
To mount a regular file, first attach it with
.Xr loopctl 8 .
A loop device attached with
.Fl r
is mounted read-only regardless of the requested options.
.Pp
The kernel honours or records only
.Ql ro ,
.Ql nosuid ,
.Ql nodev ,
.Ql noexec ,
.Ql noatime ,
.Ql nodiratime ,
.Ql relatime ,
and
.Ql silent
flags.
.Ql remount
changes those flags on a mount, as
.Xr mount 2
describes: ext2 and tmpfs change between
.Ql ro
and
.Ql rw ,
and tmpfs takes a new
.Ql size= .
.Ql bind
and
.Ql rbind
show a directory at another place, the second with the mounts below it,
as
.Xr mount 2
describes, and
.Ql remount,bind
changes the flags of that one mount.
Other flags are rejected, including those requested by
.Ql move .
.Pa /proc/mounts
records each mount with six fields in fstab format, its options
.Ql ro
or
.Ql rw
and whichever of
.Ql nosuid ,
.Ql nodev ,
.Ql noexec ,
.Ql noatime ,
.Ql nodiratime
and
.Ql relatime
are set;
.Ql silent
and the file system's own options are not shown.
.Pp
The
.Nm umount
command detaches a file system.
The kernel waits for operations in progress to finish before detaching.
An open file on the volume, or a loop device attached to a file on it,
prevents unmounting.
A mounted USB stick that has been removed can be unmounted;
buffers that can no longer be written are discarded.
.Sh OPTIONS
The
.Nm mount
options are:
.Bl -tag -width "-t fstype"
.It Fl a
Mount the file systems in
.Pa /etc/fstab ,
skipping
.Ql noauto
and swap entries, occupied mount points and the entries
.Fl t
or
.Fl O
exclude;
.Fl T
selects another table.
.It Fl f
Perform a dry run.
.It Fl v
Produce verbose output.
.It Fl r
Mount read-only.
.It Fl t Ar fstype
Select the file-system type.
.It Fl T Ar file
Read the specified table instead of
.Pa /etc/fstab .
.It Fl O Ar option
With
.Fl a ,
mount only file systems with the specified option.
.It Fl o Ar option
Specify mount options.
BusyBox recognizes
.Ql sync ,
.Ql async ,
.Ql atime ,
.Ql noatime ,
.Ql diratime ,
.Ql nodiratime ,
.Ql relatime ,
.Ql norelatime ,
.Ql dev ,
.Ql nodev ,
.Ql exec ,
.Ql noexec ,
.Ql suid ,
.Ql nosuid ,
.Ql ro ,
.Ql rw ,
.Ql remount ,
.Ql bind ,
.Ql rbind ,
.Ql move ,
.Ql shared ,
.Ql rshared ,
.Ql slave ,
.Ql rslave ,
.Ql private ,
.Ql rprivate ,
and
.Ql unbindable .
Recognition by BusyBox does not imply kernel support;
the accepted kernel flags are listed above.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /proc/mounts
.It Pa /etc/fstab
File-system table.
.It Pa /proc/mounts
Current mounts and their options.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl mount -t vfat /dev/disk0p1 /mnt
.Dl umount /mnt
After attaching an ext2 image to loop device 0:
.Dl mount -t ext2 /dev/loop0 /mnt
.Dl umount /mnt
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The kernel reports these errors:
.Bl -tag -width ENAMETOOLONG
.It Er ENODEV
The file-system type is unknown.
.It Er EINVAL
A mount flag is unsupported, or the target is the root of the root file system.
.It Er ENOTDIR
The target is not a directory.
.It Er EBUSY
The target is already a mount point; the source range is mounted or has
an open descriptor permitting writes; or an unmount was attempted while
a file or loop device still referred to the volume.
.It Er ENAMETOOLONG
The target path is 256 bytes or longer.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr proc 5 ,
.Xr disk 7 ,
.Xr loopctl 8
